{{!
    @template paygw_ifthenpay/steps

    An ordered list of short instructions, each numbered by a badge.

    Used for both the ifthenpay subscription steps and the Moodle payment-setup steps. The markup
    lives here rather than in the language strings so that translators only ever see prose, and a
    restyle touches one file instead of every language pack.

    Marked up as a real <ol> so assistive technology announces the count and position. The number
    badge is left readable rather than aria-hidden: list-style is removed for the custom marker,
    and some screen readers drop list semantics when it is, so the visible number is the reliable
    signal either way.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * badgeclass - Full Bootstrap colour pair for the number badge, background and foreground both,
      e.g. "bg-primary text-white". Named in full rather than derived from the background: Boost's
      $secondary is a light grey, so text-white on it measures 1.49:1.
    * steps - List of {number, text}; text may contain inline links and emphasis.

    Optional context variables:
    * footer - Trailing HTML, e.g. a row of documentation links.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "badgeclass": "bg-primary text-white",
        "steps": [
            {"number": 1, "text": "Subscribe and sign the contract."},
            {"number": 2, "text": "Enter the Backoffice Key below."}
        ],
        "footer": "<a href=\"https://ifthenpay.com\">ifthenpay.com</a>"
    }
}}
<ol class="list-unstyled mb-0">
    {{#steps}}
        <li class="d-flex align-items-start mb-2">
            {{! me-*/mr-* are the Bootstrap 5 and 4 spelling of the same spacing; both are emitted
                throughout this plugin so the layout holds on Moodle 4.3-4.5 and on 5.x. }}
            <span class="badge {{badgeclass}} rounded-circle me-2 mr-2 flex-shrink-0">{{number}}</span>
            <div>{{{text}}}</div>
        </li>
    {{/steps}}
</ol>
{{#footer}}
    <p class="small text-muted mt-2 mb-0">{{{.}}}</p>
{{/footer}}
